      "writtenOn": "2026-07-24T19:35:14Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "I would suggest rephrasing this a bit (comments below for more explanation):\n\n\u003e Skia Perf is a web application for analyzing and viewing performance metrics produced by performance tests run in Continuous Integration (CI/postsubmit) builds.\n\u003e\n\u003e See the main [Skia Perf docs](https://skia.googlesource.com/buildbot/+/refs/heads/main/perf/README.md) for more information.\n\u003e\n\u003e See [Skia\u0027s instance of Skia Perf, skia-perf.luci.app](https://skia-perf.luci.app/) for Skia performance results.\n\u003e\n\u003e Skia Perf was originally developed for use by the Skia project, but is now used by multiple open source projects.  It retains the name Skia Perf for now, even though it is no longer specific to Skia.\"\n\n* This makes the link to the main docs a bit more prominent.\n* This drops the link to https://perf.skia.org from the first paragraph, moves it, and makes it to be for https://skia-perf.luci.app/, which is what https://perf.skia.org redirects to anyway.\n   * While you could keep the link as https://perf.skia.org, IMO it\u0027s harder to understand what sites do what when redirects are involved.",
      "revId": "1c5eb13965c12c74f0cbd0aec52a8784aeaeba84",
      "serverId": "5086850b-e599-37d2-8ec8-ff16aeccbf02"
    },
